 "title": "Movement along the demand curve and a shift of it",
 "caption": "A change in the good's own price moves buyers along the curve. A change in anything else, such as a rise in petrol prices, shifts the whole curve: at £60 buyers now want 60 cars, not 40.",
 "alt": "Two downward-sloping demand curves. At a price of £60 the quantity demanded is 40 on the first and 60 on the shifted curve; a price rise to £80 moves along the first curve to 20.",
 "description": [
  "The first demand curve slopes down: at £60, 40 units; at £80, 20 units.",
  "A rise in the price moves buyers up the curve to a lower quantity: a movement along.",
  "A rise in the price of a substitute shifts the curve right: at £60, 60 units are now demanded."
 ],
